{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     course-card — ported from the .ns-ccard in NSDS templates/course-listing.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ONE course card, for the same reason there is ONE post-card: the last
     theme grew two that diverged. If a surface needs a different card it
     needs a different NSDS component, not a copy of this one.

     ⚠ NOT post-card. A .ns-bcard answers "is this worth reading" — cover,
     excerpt, date, reading time. A .ns-ccard answers "is this worth
     enrolling in" — level, how many lessons, how far in you already are.
     Same grid, different question, and NSDS draws them differently.

     ── EVERY FIGURE IS COUNTED, NEVER TYPED ────────────────────────────────
     The lesson count is a {{#get}} over the collection, not a number in the
     editor. partials/home/courses.hbs is still ⚠ DUMMY and hard-codes its
     levels; this is what replaces that pattern, not an extension of it.

     The filter leans on THE ONE RULE from routes.yaml — a parent post's slug
     equals its own tag's slug — so {{slug}} here is also the tag every one
     of its lessons carries as primary. Break that rule and this silently
     counts zero.

     Level is drawn ONLY when a #level-* tag is set, matching
     partials/post/training-lesson.hbs. A course with no level stated gets no
     chip rather than a guessed one.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<article class="ns-card ns-ccard">
    <span class="ns-ccard__mediawrap">
        {{#if feature_image}}
            <img class="ns-card__media" src="{{img_url feature_image size="m"}}"
                 srcset="{{img_url feature_image size="s"}} 300w, {{img_url feature_image size="m"}} 600w, {{img_url feature_image size="l"}} 1000w"
                 sizes="(min-width: 900px) 400px, 100vw"
                 alt="{{#if feature_image_alt}}{{feature_image_alt}}{{/if}}" loading="lazy">
        {{else}}
            <span class="ns-card__media ns-ph" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {{/if}}
        {{#has tag="#level-beginner"}}<span class="ns-tag ns-ccard__level">{{t "Beginner"}}</span>{{/has}}
        {{#has tag="#level-intermediate"}}<span class="ns-tag ns-ccard__level">{{t "Intermediate"}}</span>{{/has}}
        {{#has tag="#level-advanced"}}<span class="ns-tag ns-ccard__level">{{t "Advanced"}}</span>{{/has}}
        {{#has tag="#updated"}}<span class="ns-ccard__badge ns-ccard__badge--updated">{{t "Updated"}}</span>{{/has}}
    </span>

    <div class="ns-card__body">
        <span class="ns-card__kicker">{{t "// Course"}}</span>
        {{!-- The link wraps the heading, not the card — a card-wide link
             swallows the level chip and the meta row inside it. --}}
        <a class="ns-card__link" href="{{url}}"><h3 class="ns-card__title">{{title}}</h3></a>
        {{#if excerpt}}<p class="ns-card__text">{{excerpt words="20"}}</p>{{/if}}
        <span class="ns-ccard__meta">
            {{#get "posts" filter="primary_tag:{{slug}}+tag:hash-lesson" limit="1"}}
                <span>{{pagination.total}} {{t "lessons"}}</span>
            {{/get}}
            <span><time datetime="{{date format="YYYY-MM-DD"}}">{{date format="MMM YYYY"}}</time></span>
        </span>
    </div>
</article>
